  {
   "op": "note",
   "uid": "s-shelter",
   "text": "The Tag House: an open HTBM half pavilion on a levelled pad is the handover shelter, its front north onto two ways that end at its two front corners. The arrival half (west, toward the Rose) has closed baskets and chimes hung from the eave for the tags; the departure half (east, toward the villages) has the wicker bench, wrapped bundles and urns. Three candle stands run across the floor between the halves. The keeper's hut (HTBM bamboohut02, linked cell) stands east on the villages' side, chimes on its eave."
  }
